Description: Optional read-only debugfs dump of the EC PWM registers
 pwmN/pwmN_enable are a driver cache (D4); whether the EC really holds a
 written duty could only be checked with the userspace tool n5_i2ec_read,
 which uses ioperm() and bypasses the driver lock (C2). This adds a
 validation view inside the driver.
 .
 New module parameter debug_regs (bool, 0444, default N). With N there is
 no debugfs entry and no Super-I/O access at all. With Y, and only on a
 matched board profile whose DMI sys_vendor is the measured "Micro
 Computer (HK) Tech Limited", the probe creates
 <debugfs>/minisforum_n5_it5571/dcr (mode 0400, seq_file, read only, no
 write/ioctl/mmap). On a force-loaded unknown system or a vendor mismatch
 debug_regs=1 is ignored with a warning: every read writes the Super-I/O
 index and the I2EC address registers, which must not happen on
 unidentified hardware (delta review N1, same class as A2). A failed
 debugfs_create_dir/file (debugfs=off, -EEXIST) is logged and leaves no
 entry. Reading the file returns I2EC 0x1800-0x180f (0x1801 CTR,
 0x1802-0x1809 DCR0-7) in the format of "n5_i2ec_read 0x1800 16".
 .
 Access: the same port sequence as upstream research-tools/n5_i2ec_read.c
 (feb6d9a, blob 1de90e3): Super-I/O index 0x2e/data 0x2f, depth-2
 registers D2ADR 0x2e/D2DAT 0x2f, I2EC address 0x11 (high), 0x10 (low),
 data 0x12. Upstream uses no Super-I/O enter/exit key sequence for this
 EC and none is added: the sequence is the one used on the reference host
 for all I2EC snapshots, an unmeasured key sequence would be new port
 writes (including SIO register 0x02). The ports are taken with
 request_muxed_region(0x2e, 2) for every read and released afterwards,
 under data->lock. There are no status waits (I2EC is direct), so no wait
 bound is needed; one read is 16 x 12 port accesses. Address and length
 are compile-time constants; there is no function that writes the I2EC
 data register (G3). After a read the Super-I/O index points to D2DAT and
 the I2EC address to 0x180f, as with the upstream tool (accepted, a reset
 would be another unmeasured port write).
 .
 Kernel lockdown (integrity or confidentiality) does not block this file:
 debugfs lets 0400 files without write/ioctl/mmap through
 (v7.0 fs/debugfs/file.c, debugfs_locked_down()).
 .
 Resolves D4 (live value available for validation), makes B9 possible
 (read-back after write, by the tester; B9 stays N/A for the driver, which
 does not read back automatically). B6: request_muxed_region is used; the
 missing enter/exit sequence is a justified deviation (see above). G5 met
 (parameter off by default, file read-only, vendor-gated). G3 stays PASS.
 debug_regs must never be set in modprobe.d (validation only).
 .
 Tested: build/static analysis as 0001; modinfo lists debug_regs. Not
 tested on hardware: dcr output vs. n5_i2ec_read 0x1800 16 (n5-fangov
 stopped, module loaded with debug_regs=1), /proc/ioports during a read.
